      "family": "tonic-less in major, tonic-ful in minor",
      "corpus_sections": 2,
      "note": "The verse is Am-F-Dm-Am (roots 6,4,2,6 in Hookpad's C major file), so the set has two readings: ii-IV-vi with no tonic in C, or i-VI-iv WITH the tonic in A minor. Which one you hear depends on landing on Am, and the verse both starts and ends there. RARE: only 2 sections in the corpus use exactly this set — this one and the Shins' 'Caring Is Creepy' bridge. Not because it hides in minor: the set i-iv-VI appears 0 times in minor-notated sections. The corpus is 2896 major-notated sections to 110 minor, so relative-minor passages live inside major files sitting on vi. Shares degrees with 'starlight' (Muse, Bennett) but that is an ordered loop ii-vi-IV; this is the unordered set.",
